# Facts carry concrete boundary partitions. The formulas are authored descriptions, not copied implementations.
FACTS = {
'lookback-boundary':('promql/engine.go','vectorSelectorSingle','Instant selector selects last sample <=target, but a prior sample at or before target-lookback is excluded: the lookback lower boundary is OPEN. A stale float or histogram Sum stale marker excludes the series and does not search through that marker.',['target-lookback-1ms','target-lookback','target-lookback+1ms','target','target+1ms']),
'number-conversion':('promql/parser/parse.go','func (p *parser) number','Number parsing first attempts base-inferred int64 and converts it to binary64; otherwise binary64 parsing applies. Decimal exponent notation and numeric underscores must pass both lexer and conversion. Hex integers are accepted, hex floating-point literals are rejected by the lexer. Inf/NaN are case-insensitive lexical keywords.',['0','-0','0x10','0X_FF','1_024','1e-3','1e','0x1.8p1','1__2','1e309']),
'string-escapes':('promql/parser/lex.go','func lexEscape','Escaped quotes/backslash and a,b,f,n,r,t,v are accepted. Octal byte escapes require 3 digits <=255; hex bytes 2 digits; Unicode uses 4 or 8 hex digits, excluding surrogate range D800-DFFF and values >10FFFF. Quoted newline/EOF is unterminated; raw backtick strings admit newlines without interpreting escapes. Invalid UTF-8 is rejected.',['\\000','\\377','\\400','\\x00','\\uD7FF','\\uD800','\\uE000','\\U0010FFFF','\\U00110000','unterminated quote','raw newline']),
'rate-extrapolation':('promql/functions.go','func extrapolatedRate','Require at least two same-kind observations and remove mixed float/hist windows with warning. Difference last-first is counter-corrected by adding the previous value for each decrease. Let observed span S and mean gap A=S/(n-1). Each edge gap >=1.1*A is replaced by A/2; otherwise keep it. Counter float extrapolation toward start is capped at estimated time to zero when first>=0 and corrected difference>0. Multiply difference by (S+leftGap+rightGap)/S; rate additionally divides by requested range seconds.',['0 samples','1 sample','2 samples','edge 1.1*A-1ms','edge 1.1*A','counter reset','zero crossing','mixed kind']),
'regression':('promql/functions.go','func linearRegression','Use seconds relative to intercept time and compensated sums X,Y,XY,X²; slope=(sumXY-sumX*sumY/n)/(sumX²-sumX²/n), intercept=meanY-slope*meanX. Constant finite series has slope 0 and original intercept; constant infinity returns NaN slope/intercept. deriv needs >=2 floats; predict_linear returns intercept+slope*horizon.',['one float','two floats','constant finite','constant +Inf','opposite infinities','NaN','large epoch with small gaps']),
'float-sum-mean':('promql/functions.go','func funcAvgOverTime','Float sums use compensated accumulation, not arbitrary reordering. Means use compensated sum/count until overflow and then incremental mean updates; opposite infinities/NaN propagate through arithmetic. Population variance divides by N, not N-1. Irregular spacing does not change weights.',['single value','large cancellation','overflowing finite sum','same-sign infinity','opposite infinities','NaN','uneven timestamp spacing']),
'round-clamp':('promql/functions.go','func funcRound','round computes floor(value*(1/nearest)+0.5)/(1/nearest), nearest defaults to 1; nearest zero/Inf/NaN follows that exact binary64 expression. clamp with min>max returns empty; NaN bound yields NaN; native histogram samples are ignored.',['nearest 0','nearest -0','nearest -2','nearest Inf','nearest NaN','half tie +/-','min=max','min>max','NaN bound']),
'smoothing':('promql/functions.go','func funcDoubleExponentialSmoothing','Require >=2 floats. Level starts at first float, trend at second-first; each next level uses sf*value+(1-sf)*(previousLevel+updatedTrend), with trend combining tf*(previousLevel-olderLevel)+(1-tf)*priorTrend after initial trend. Factors <=0 or >=1 raise invalid-parameter error. NaN factors pass these comparisons and propagate numerically rather than being explicitly rejected.',['sf=0','sf=1','sf=nextafter(0,+Inf)','sf=nextafter(1,0)','sf=NaN','tf=0','tf=1','one float','mixed float/hist']),
'classic-quantile':('promql/quantile.go','func BucketQuantile','Sort classic boundaries, coalesce duplicate boundaries by adding counts, ignore relative cumulative deltas <=1e-12*(abs(previous)+abs(current)), and force larger decreases up to previous cumulative value. Missing +Inf terminal, fewer than two buckets, or zero total gives NaN. For q<0/>1 return -/+Inf, q=NaN gives NaN. Rank=q*total; interpolate linearly between finite neighboring bounds, lower bound defaults 0 when first upper>0. First nonpositive bucket returns its upper bound; quantile in terminal +Inf returns previous upper. Monotonic repair is info, malformed le is warning.',['q=-1','q=0','q=1','q=2','q=NaN','missing +Inf','duplicate le','zero total','tiny negative delta','material decrease','negative first bound']),
'native-quantile':('promql/quantile.go','func HistogramQuantile','Empty histogram or NaN q yields NaN; out-of-range q yields signed infinity. Select bucket by rank; traverse forward for NaN sum or q<0.5 and backward otherwise. Clamp accumulated count to total. Interpolate custom/zero buckets linearly; nonzero exponential buckets uniformly in log2(abs(value)), respecting negative direction. Zero bucket extends only toward zero if all observations lie on one sign. Custom -Inf first bucket uses 0 lower when positive upper, otherwise returns upper; custom +Inf last bucket returns lower.',['empty','q=0','q=0.5','q=1','q=NaN','positive/negative/zero bucket','custom +/-Inf edge','count-vs-bucket mismatch']),
'native-fraction':('promql/quantile.go','func HistogramFraction','Empty histogram or NaN bounds yields NaN; lower>=upper returns 0. Compute cumulative rank at each bound using linear interpolation in zero/custom buckets or log2 interpolation in exponential buckets; divide upper-minus-lower rank by total count. Clamp bound ranks to observed total; +/-Inf naturally bound all buckets. NaN observations count toward histogram total but not finite bucket rank.',['empty','equal bounds','reversed bounds','NaN bound','-Inf,+Inf','bound exactly bucket edge','negative log bucket','zero bucket','NaN observations']),
'histogram-scale':('model/histogram/float_histogram.go','func (h *FloatHistogram) Mul','Scaling multiplies bucket populations, count, sum and zero count. Negative scaling/division marks gauge. Divide by zero constructs histogram with no ordinary buckets and zero population/count/sum becoming +/-Inf or NaN according to original numerator. Histogram values are not converted into ordinary float samples.',['factor -1','factor -0','factor 0','factor NaN','factor Inf','denominator 0','denominator -0']),
'histogram-reset':('model/histogram/float_histogram.go','func (h *FloatHistogram) DetectReset','Explicit reset hint wins true and not-reset hint wins false. Otherwise detect decreased total count, incompatible schema-kind, increased resolution, decreased zero threshold, a larger zero threshold that cuts a populated previous bucket, reduced adjusted zero count, disappeared populated bucket or any decreased comparable bucket. Gauge flavor alone is not an equality change.',['explicit reset','explicit not-reset','count decrease','resolution increase/decrease','zero threshold split','disappeared populated bucket','empty disappearing bucket']),
'utc-calendar':('promql/functions.go','func dateWrapper','Calendar functions default to evaluation time if vector argument omitted; vector values are truncated to integer Unix seconds before UTC conversion. day_of_week is Sunday=0 through Saturday=6; day_of_month 1..31; day_of_year 1..366; month 1..12; hour0..23; minute0..59; days_in_month uses Gregorian leap-year rules. Histograms ignored.',['epoch','-0.9 seconds','leap Feb 2000','nonleap Feb 2100','year boundary','omitted argument','empty vector']),
'quantile-values':('promql/quantile.go','func quantile','Ordinary quantile over floats sorts NaNs before finite values; for 0<=q<=1 use rank=q*(N-1) and linear interpolation between floor/ceil rank values. q=NaN gives NaN and out-of-range gives signed infinity; zero values gives NaN in the helper but a missing window emits no series.',['N=0','N=1','N=2','q=0','q=0.5','q=1','q=NaN','NaN observation']),
'matching-labels':('promql/engine.go','func resultMetric','For one-to-one matching, on retains only matching labels, ignoring removes ignored labels. For grouped matching, base labels come from many side and include labels from one side; missing/empty included label deletes it. Arithmetic removes metric name even if on(__name__) lists it. Duplicate result label sets are errors.',['empty on()','on(__name__)','ignoring absent label','group_left include absent','duplicate one side','duplicate output']),
'absent-derived-labels':('promql/functions.go','func createLabelsForAbsentFunction','absent derivation uses only non-metric-name equality matchers; duplicate equality matchers for a label remove that label from derived output rather than selecting one. Non-selector expressions do not invent argument labels. absent_over_time accepts any observed sample kind as presence.',['empty selector result','duplicate equality label','regex matcher','__name__ equality','nonselector input','histogram-only presence'])}
